{
  "dom_id": "step-q187261",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Complete the ratio table below.\n\n| $4$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- |\n| $8$ | $24$ |\n| {{field-2}} | $27$ |",
  "worked_solution": "We start with the ratio $8:24$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{24}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the left-hand entry ($8$), and the denominator represents the right-hand entry ($24$).\n\nNow we divide the numerator and the denominator by $8$ to find an equivalent ratio:\n\n$$\n\\frac{8÷8}{24÷8}=\\frac{1}{3}\n$$\n\nWe can generate equivalent ratios by finding equivalent fractions:\n\n- To create a numerator of $4,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator of our fraction by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1\\times 4}{3\\times 4}=\\frac{4}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To create a denominator of $27,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator of our fraction by $9:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1\\times 9}{3\\times 9} & =\\frac{9}{27}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we fill in the ratio table:\n\n| $4$ | $12$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $8$ | $24$ |\n| $9$ | $27$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
